      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "2026-07-19 — “ruminate” already does this work for me. To ruminate is, literally, to chew again. The vocabulary of digestion is sitting inside the vocabulary of thought, waiting to be noticed and tended.",
        "sourceId": "notes-2",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 14
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aT0n6",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "binding:K-ZRVOgAVbet-KFHULB3t": {
      "meta": {},
      "id": "binding:K-ZRVOgAVbet-KFHULB3t",
      "type": "arrow",
      "fromId": "shape:TRKsx0kfi8iWgIaEDj7E3",
      "toId": "shape:8DPp92e2PS_jbLflCX9VP",
      "props": {
        "isPrecise": false,
        "isExact": false,
        "normalizedAnchor": {
          "x": 0.5,
          "y": 0.5
        },
        "snap": "none",
        "terminal": "end"
      },
      "typeName": "binding"
    },
    "shape:iuWyBjV_M67suiHyd0gqI": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 1016,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:iuWyBjV_M67suiHyd0gqI",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:m_JQs1vh7ev7ZFEm4X4p1",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "Information is abundant and attention is the bottleneck.",
        "sourceId": "r-009",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 9
      },
      "index": "a9OCj",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "user:Kx517dozKBGzRhGewsYgI": {
      "name": "",
      "color": "#BD54C6",
      "imageUrl": "",
      "meta": {},
      "id": "user:Kx517dozKBGzRhGewsYgI",
      "typeName": "user"
    },
    "shape:Q6v7BwU_-f-xUqXudax6g": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 272,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Q6v7BwU_-f-xUqXudax6g",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:m_JQs1vh7ev7ZFEm4X4p1",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "Rest is the only cure, so we are told to unplug, to detox, to abstain.",
        "sourceId": "r-003",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 3
      },
      "index": "a3cJU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:Mj-wgi5H69D9UQ97MvI_x": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 992,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Mj-wgi5H69D9UQ97MvI_x",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "2026-07-14 — the wallet metaphor is Puritan in disguise: spend wisely, save diligently, guard the balance. It smuggles in a whole ethics of scarcity that the digestive metaphor simply refuses.",
        "sourceId": "notes-1",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 13
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aSIUo",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:Gyu4lpEnHnvSXkD86lRby": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 48,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Gyu4lpEnHnvSXkD86lRby",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "move",
        "text": "Picture the gut, not the wallet—the figure worth carrying is a long, coiled, patient organ that does not care how much arrives at once so much as what it is asked to break down, and how well it was fed in the years before the test.",
        "sourceId": "f-007",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 7
      },
      "parentId": "shape:OrypP3apbvLqca33-xLSd",
      "index": "a1",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:ULOq5Jfye58rdSk1wA3nP": {
      "x": 392,
      "y": 272,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:ULOq5Jfye58rdSk1wA3nP",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:qSBVHYUr_ji9QkO3ClHZd",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "claim",
        "text": "The discipline is not withdrawal but composition — choosing a diet the mind can actually digest.",
        "sourceId": "m-004",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 4
      },
      "index": "a47cn",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:BTm0tzXLruKvp1vGo5p5F": {
